  "human_edit_summary": "Task-stage evidence re-bind after the quality gate flipped T-002 from `Implementation Complete` to `Done` (PASS, ledger seq 670). That lifecycle flip changed the raw bytes of tasks.md, and the binding recorded by attempt-5 was the raw bytes of the prior state (9d88304142b01219ea4935a2753153af84ddc098edfd9a26e0dce2b2f51d26cc = the raw sha256 of tasks.md at commit 94594c51), so check-workflow-state.sh reported `task plan hash is stale`. This attempt is likewise a RAW-BYTES binding, not a normalized one: the plan is status-mixed (T-001 and T-002 `Done`, T-003..T-010 `Planned`), and each of the three normalizing forms the validator accepts rewrites every `Status:` line to one uniform value, so none of them can reproduce a mixed-status file. Only the raw form matches, and it will go stale again on the next lifecycle flip. This is the fourth feature in this session to hit the defect; WFI-025 is filed against the root cause and is mid-audit. No content of tasks.md was edited — the sole diff since the last bind is T-002 `Status: Implementation Complete` -> `Status: Done` (git diff 94594c51..33e1b04c). Both reviewers verified that diff independently. SECOND RE-BIND (same attempt-6/round-1 record, no new review performed): after T-003/T-004/T-005 each flipped `Status: Planned` -> `Status: Implementation Complete` (commits e8ffc4c9, 56155686, 472579a3), the raw-bytes pin above (d30c0513db48b922a62f9e957b67c2820f43d477407bd8c5a451b8ed5e328476) went stale exactly as predicted, reproducing `task plan hash is stale`. Per the quality-gate T-002 report's own recorded remedy table (reports/quality-gate/epic-193-a5-capability-resolver/T-002.md), this record now pins `normalized_hash(tasks.md, task)` instead (38770deaf590060af86a7043224e2c202bed13dfb6b84ee21d6e98885abd815c): every `Status:` line rewritten uniformly to `Planned`, `Task-Review-Status:` to `Pending`, `Approval:` to `Draft`, `Second Approval:` lines dropped. This form is invariant under per-task lifecycle flips by construction (it discards Status/Approval bookkeeping entirely, keeping only body content), so it will not go stale on T-006..T-010's remaining transitions the way the raw and rereview_normalized_hash forms structurally cannot survive a mixed-status file. Confirmed independently: recomputing this normalized form from the current tasks.md (T-001/T-002 Done, T-003/T-004/T-005 Implementation Complete, T-006..T-010 Planned) reproduces the identical value the T-002 report computed before those three flips existed, proving no tasks.md body content changed across either transition. No content of tasks.md was edited by this re-bind and no reviewer manifest input other than the `tasks.md` entries above changed.",
